  "pathwayDescription": "The Vietnam Energy Outlook Report is a governmental publication, developed by the Electricity and Renewable Energy Authority (EREA) in collaboration with external partners, that provides multiple potential pathways for Vietnam's energy sector. The Baseline scenario represents a business-as-usual trajectory of Vietnam's energy system development. Specifically, the scenario portrays how the energy system evolves if no new policy action is taken beyond existing plans and commitments, where GHG reductions are not prioritized, and where the net-zero energy target by 2050 is not met. The scenario is optimized toward the lowest possible total system cost while meeting growing energy demand, showing that even without explicit emissions reduction policies, some decarbonization occurs due to efficiency gains and declining costs of renewables. However, in the absence of strong policy action, emissions continue to rise until 2030, expanding fossil-based infrastructure and delaying significant system transition. Power sector emissions peak at 173 Mt in 2030 and significantly exceed projections in EREA's Net Zero and Net Zero+ scenarios. By 2050, total energy sector emissions are more than double the emissions in the Net Zero pathway.",
